# ArticleCard

Article preview for listings and related articles, not article body content. Full-bleed image, gradient, date, title, and author; one React Router link.

File: `app/articles/ArticleCard.tsx`

## Props

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `href` | `string` | Required | Full article destination |
| `title` | `string` | Required | Article title |
| `image` | `string` | Required | Background image URL |
| `description` | `string` | — | Short excerpt |
| `imageAlt` | `string` | `title` | Meaningful image alt text |
| `date` | `string` | — | Formatted date |
| `datetime` | `string` | — | ISO date for `<time>` |
| `author` | `Author` | — | Name and avatar |
| `ctaText` | `string` | `"Read more"` | CTA label; empty string hides it |
| `className` | `string` | — | Additional classes |
| `variant` | `"default" \| "compact"` | `"default"` | Card size |

## Semantic Hints

`card`, `article-card`, `preview`, `teaser`, `post-card`, `blog-card`, `article-preview`, `content-card`

## Behavior and Accessibility

Use a 16:9 card with bottom-aligned content and a transparent-to-dark gradient. Keep the title prominent and text contrast sufficient. Compact cards have reduced width and padding. Provide hover feedback and a visible keyboard focus outline. The CTA is a span, never a nested button or link. React uses `dateTime` for the HTML `datetime` attribute.

## Implementation

```tsx
import { Link } from "react-router";

type Author = {
  name: string;
  avatar: string;
};

type ArticleCardProps = {
  href: string;
  title: string;
  image: string;
  description?: string;
  imageAlt?: string;
  date?: string;
  datetime?: string;
  author?: Author;
  ctaText?: string;
  className?: string;
  variant?: "default" | "compact";
};

export function ArticleCard({
  href,
  title,
  image,
  description,
  imageAlt = title,
  date,
  datetime,
  author,
  ctaText = "Read more",
  className = "",
  variant = "default",
}: ArticleCardProps) {
  const compact = variant === "compact";

  return (
    <article
      className={`relative aspect-video overflow-hidden ${className}`}
      style={{ maxWidth: compact ? 360 : undefined }}
    >
      <img
        src={image}
        alt={imageAlt}
        className="absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover"
      />
      <div
        aria-hidden="true"
        className="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-b from-transparent to-black"
      />
      <Link
        to={href}
        className="absolute inset-0 flex flex-col justify-end text-white hover:shadow-inner focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-[-4px]"
        style={{ padding: compact ? 12 : 24 }}
      >
        {date && <time dateTime={datetime}>{date}</time>}
        <h2 className="text-xl font-bold">{title}</h2>
        {description && <p>{description}</p>}
        {author && (
          <span className="flex items-center gap-2">
            <img
              src={author.avatar}
              alt=""
              className="h-8 w-8 rounded-full"
            />
            {author.name}
          </span>
        )}
        {ctaText && <span>{ctaText}</span>}
      </Link>
    </article>
  );
}

// Render inside an existing React Router route.
const example = (
  <ArticleCard
    href="/articles/machine-learning-basics"
    title="Getting Started with Machine Learning"
    image="/images/ml-basics.jpg"
    date="January 15, 2024"
    datetime="2024-01-15"
    author={{ name: "Jane Smith", avatar: "/avatars/jane.jpg" }}
  />
);
```

