# HeroSection

## Purpose
Reusable page hero for React Router listing, category, and other prominent page headers. For article content, use `ArticleHeroHeader` instead.

## Props
| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `title` (required) | `string` | — | Main heading text |
| `description` | `string` | — | Subtitle/description text |
| `children` | `ReactNode` | — | Additional content: buttons, search, etc. |
| `className` | `string` | — | Additional CSS classes |
| `variant` | `"primary" \| "secondary" \| "neutral"` | `"primary"` | Color variant |

## Semantic Hints
`hero`, `header`, `banner`, `page-header`, `page-hero`, `headline`, `masthead`, `jumbotron`

## Structure and Styling
Wrapper → named section → constrained-width container → text container → heading, optional description, optional children wrapper.

Use full-width backgrounds, responsive `text-3xl`–`text-5xl` headings, `py-12`–`py-16` padding, comfortable description line height, and separated child content. Tailwind utilities below are illustrative, not established project tokens.

| Variant | Use case | Colors |
|---|---|---|
| `primary` | Main pages | Brand background; indigo in this example |
| `secondary` | Secondary pages | Lighter brand background |
| `neutral` | Minimal pages | Gray/white background |

