## Semantic Hints

`resource-cta`, `download-cta`, `pdf-cta`, `guide-cta`, `lead-magnet`, `gated-content`, `resource-download`

## Implementation

Render within the project's React Router context. Use `Link` with `reloadDocument` so resource requests bypass client-side routing. The `download` attribute requests a download; cross-origin behavior also depends on server headers.

```tsx
import { Link } from "react-router";

type ArticleResourceDownloadProps = {
  topic: string;
  title?: string;
  description?: string;
  buttonLabel?: string;
  buttonHref?: string;
  eyebrow?: string;
  className?: string;
  previewImages?: string[];
};

export function ArticleResourceDownload({
  topic,
  title = `${topic} Checklist & Notes`,
  description = "Download a practical checklist and notes for your next project.",
  buttonLabel = "Download Checklist (PDF)",
  buttonHref = "#",
  eyebrow = "Free download",
  className = "",
  previewImages = [],
}: ArticleResourceDownloadProps) {
  return (
    <section className={`relative overflow-hidden rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-br from-indigo-50 to-white p-8 text-slate-900 ${className}`}>
      <div
        aria-hidden="true"
        className="pointer-events-none absolute -right-8 top-0 h-48 w-48 rounded-full bg-indigo-200 blur-3xl"
      />
      <div className="relative grid items-center gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
        <div>
          <span className="text-sm font-semibold uppercase text-indigo-800">
